From: Avocado Linux <info@avocadolinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] wiringpi.i: use SWIG_AppendOutput in the argout typemap

SWIG 4.3 gave SWIG_Python_AppendOutput a third parameter:

  SWIG_Python_AppendOutput(PyObject *result, PyObject *obj, int is_void);

so this typemap's two-argument call no longer compiles against the runtime
SWIG itself generates into the wrapper (swig 4.4.1 here):

  wiringpi_wrap.c:6112:17: error: too few arguments to function
  'SWIG_Python_AppendOutput'; expected 3, have 2

SWIG's own upgrade note for that change says to use SWIG_AppendOutput
instead; Lib/python/pytypemaps.swg defines it as

  #define SWIG_AppendOutput(result, obj) SWIG_Python_AppendOutput(result, obj, $isvoid)

which fills in the $isvoid the typemap cannot know by itself. This is the
idiom upstream's own Examples/python/multimap/example.i uses, and it works
on SWIG 4.2 and earlier too, where SWIG_AppendOutput expands to the
two-argument form.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor fork, rubikpi-ai/WiringRP-Python]
---
--- a/wiringpi.i
+++ b/wiringpi.i
@@ -286,7 +286,7 @@
 };
 
 %typemap(argout) (unsigned char *data) {
-      $result = SWIG_Python_AppendOutput($result, PyString_FromStringAndSize((char *) $1, result));
+      $result = SWIG_AppendOutput($result, PyString_FromStringAndSize((char *) $1, result));
 };
 
 %include "bindings.i"
